1
00:00:00,206 --> 00:00:03,034
That QR code on your menu
could stop working tomorrow,

2
00:00:03,074 --> 00:00:04,805
and nobody would warn you.

3
00:00:05,223 --> 00:00:08,855
Many free QR makers send your
code through their own server.

4
00:00:08,895 --> 00:00:12,061
When the trial ends,
every printed copy fails.

5
00:00:12,477 --> 00:00:15,676
Meet QR Check. See who
really controls your codes.

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,035
Scan a code with the camera, upload
a photo, or paste what it says.

7
00:00:20,455 --> 00:00:23,340
It draws the chain, from the
printed code to your page,

8
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:26,122
and marks the middleman
who holds the switch.

9
00:00:26,538 --> 00:00:28,000
This is a hosted QR code.

10
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:32,955
Whoever runs that service decides where
it goes, and the fix is spelled out.

11
00:00:33,379 --> 00:00:35,733
Save each code with where it is printed.

12
00:00:37,262 --> 00:00:41,481
Codes that rely on a middleman go
straight to the top, ready to replace.

13
00:00:41,905 --> 00:00:45,083
Then make a direct code that
nobody else can switch off.

14
00:00:48,049 --> 00:00:50,633
Every code is read back
the moment it is drawn,

15
00:00:50,673 --> 00:00:52,866
to prove it says exactly what you typed.

16
00:00:52,906 --> 00:00:54,986
Then print a sheet of stickers.

17
00:00:55,406 --> 00:00:59,647
QR Check. Free, offline, and no
account. Check your codes today.
